1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
In this tutorial video, we use the 11th version of Doshi Marvelous Designer.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
If you need to learn the 10th version of Marvelous Designer, please watch the previous video.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
In order to make it easier to learn, the Doshi Marvelous Designer is used in this tutorial.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000
We have learned how to create clothing in Marvelous Designer through previous tutorials.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Now we will learn how to make your clothes look more real.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:40,000
You can use default fabric without modifying the fabric.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
By modifying the fabric properties, you can make your clothes look more real.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Before starting, open the 3D window to show the thickness of the fabric and the texture of the fabric.

9
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Please note that default fabric is 0.5mm thick.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Now let's apply the fabric to the clothes.

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Click on the Add button of the fabric window to add a new fabric.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Double-click on the name to modify.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Select the adjustment panel tool, then press the Shift button to select all the thick and shawl panels.

14
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Click on the application button next to the fabric.

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Apply the fabric of the newly created.

16
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:24,000
When selecting a fabric, the outline of the panel with this fabric will be displayed as orange.

17
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Select the new fabric of the T-shirt.

18
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,000
You can adjust its properties in the property editor below.

19
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
At the bottom of the property editor is the physical property.

20
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:40,000
You can change the physical properties of the fabric in it, or select the default fabric provided by Marvelous Designer.

21
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:47,000
When you select a preset fabric, the physical properties below will follow the selection and produce a change.

22
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
You can also adjust these values according to the need for manual adjustment.

23
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Here we select the preset fabric, which is Knit Pick Jersey.

24
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Select it and start the simulation.

25
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Please refer to other physical properties teaching videos for detailed explanations on physical properties.

26
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,000
After changing the physical properties, you can manually organize the panels.

27
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Next, let's take a look at the material settings.

28
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:19,000
First, you can choose a different preset type.

29
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,000
In addition, you can add the material pattern to the fabric texture.

30
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Or set the strength of the hair line or change the pattern for the fabric.

31
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Click on the color block to change the material color.

32
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:49,000
About transparency, the lower its value, the lighter the fabric, the more translucent it can be.

33
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Please note that the high-quality rendering option in the 3D window of the hook selection can be selected.

34
00:02:53,000 --> 00:03:02,000
It is better to check the material material effect.

35
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:08,000
However, as a T-shirt, it is still not transparent.

36
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
These preset fabrics can also be imported into the library.

37
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Let's try to apply preset fabric to the pocket.

38
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,000
First, add a new fabric to the fabric window.

39
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Select a new fabric.

40
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Select the adjustment panel tool and click on the pocket.

41
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Then click on the application button next to the new fabric and apply it to the panel.

42
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Then open the Fabric folder in the Library window.

43
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Here you can preview the reference effects of various fabrics and drag them onto the fabric to apply these properties.

44
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:46,000
In this video, we will use lightweight denim so that you can easily distinguish the materials.

45
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:51,000
When dragging the fabric to the newly created fabric, you will see that the name of the fabric has changed.

46
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Double-click to change it.

47
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:57,000
The fabric dragged in from the Library window will also contain materials and physical properties.

48
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:05,000
You can modify other properties in the property editor.

49
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Now we will change the material type of the fabric to Fabric Shiny.

50
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Can you feel the difference?

51
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Click on the control button to start the simulation.

52
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:21,000
After modifying the material physical properties, the wearing effect of the clothing will change.

53
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Because the physical properties will affect the stretch of the clothing, the wrinkle texture, etc.

54
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Therefore, modifying the appropriate physical properties will help the clothing look more real.

55
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Therefore, after changing the material physical properties, you can adjust the 2D version according to the effect in the 3D window.

56
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Please save your work as a project file and it will be used in the following courses.

